
# 916 Gold Guide – Understanding 22K Gold in India

## What is 916 Gold?

916 gold is 22-karat gold containing 91.6% pure gold by mass. The remaining 8.4% consists of other metals used in the alloy.

## Why is 916 Gold Popular?

- Suitable for many traditional jewellery designs.
- More durable than pure 24K gold.
- Widely used in Indian necklaces, bangles and earrings.

## Difference Between 916 and 999 Gold

| Type | Gold content |
|---|---:|
| 916 | 91.6% |
| 999 | 99.9% |

## How to Check 916 Gold Jewellery

1. Look for the applicable BIS hallmark.
2. Check the HUID where applicable.
3. Verify the hallmark using the official BIS Care app.
4. Request a detailed invoice from the seller.

Official information: https://www.bis.gov.in/

## Before Buying

Always check purity, net weight, making charges and applicable taxes before purchasing.

